WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.411 --> 00:00:08.432
Tom Lindqvist: Hey Julie, how's it going?

2
00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:15.298
Julie Hammond: Hi Tom. Good, busy. We're heading into our fall promo, so the showrooms are a little chaotic. How about you?

3
00:00:16.228 --> 00:00:25.278
Tom Lindqvist: Same here. I wanted to check in before the seasonal rush hits both of us. Is this still a decent time?

4
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:32.867
Julie Hammond: Yeah, I've got about half an hour before my next meeting. What's on your list?

5
00:00:33.356 --> 00:00:41.495
Tom Lindqvist: Mostly logistics. First, I noticed we have the PreSense refresher on the calendar for next Wednesday. Is that still good for your team?

6
00:00:42.221 --> 00:00:51.937
Julie Hammond: Wednesday works. I think we have eight people signed up right now, mostly the new hires out of the Orlando and Jacksonville stores.

7
00:00:53.157 --> 00:01:02.678
Tom Lindqvist: Okay, I'll confirm with our training team and send the join link Tuesday. Do they need the screen pop walkthrough before the session, or just the live demo?

8
00:01:03.369 --> 00:01:11.537
Julie Hammond: Just the live demo is fine. Most of them have seen it in the store, they just haven't had the formal training yet.

9
00:01:12.085 --> 00:01:19.943
Tom Lindqvist: Got it. And the AI Voice Agent tuning session we talked about, is that still something you want to schedule for early November?

10
00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:30.067
Julie Hammond: Yes, please. After the promo settles down. Maybe the second week of November? I can check with the call center leads and get back to you.

11
00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:41.041
Tom Lindqvist: Second week works on our side. Just let me know and I'll send the invite. Anything changing on the user side lately?

12
00:01:41.512 --> 00:01:50.618
Julie Hammond: We had two people leave, one on the analyst team and one on the floor in Savannah. I'll send you the deactivation list by Friday.

13
00:01:50.926 --> 00:01:55.936
Tom Lindqvist: Perfect. And do you need any help with the new hires' access once they're added?

14
00:01:56.338 --> 00:02:02.336
Julie Hammond: I don't think so. Our IT guy handles that, he's got the process down now.

15
00:02:03.793 --> 00:02:08.780
Tom Lindqvist: Good. How are call volumes looking heading into the season? Any different from last year?

16
00:02:10.017 --> 00:02:18.896
Julie Hammond: Up a bit, maybe ten percent. The AI Voice Agent has been taking a chunk of the after-hours calls, which helps.

17
00:02:18.896 --> 00:02:21.009
Julie Hammond: Store hours have been steady.

18
00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:27.899
Tom Lindqvist: Nice. Anything on the Amazon Connect side I should know about, any routing changes coming?

19
00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:35.149
Julie Hammond: Not that I've heard. We're keeping the same queues for now. If that changes, I'll loop you in.

20
00:02:36.068 --> 00:02:46.604
Tom Lindqvist: Sounds good. I'll also check in with our support team to make sure the holiday coverage is set, just in case anything comes up.

21
00:02:48.085 --> 00:02:55.463
Julie Hammond: That would be great, thanks. The last thing we need is a system hiccup during Black Friday weekend.

22
00:02:56.396 --> 00:03:02.221
Tom Lindqvist: Exactly. I'll make sure someone's on standby. Anything else you want to cover while we're here?

23
00:03:03.688 --> 00:03:12.886
Julie Hammond: I don't think so. Just the training dates and the user list. Oh, and can you send me the updated best practices doc for PreSense?

24
00:03:12.886 --> 00:03:16.197
Julie Hammond: I want to share it with the store managers.

25
00:03:16.822 --> 00:03:24.649
Tom Lindqvist: Sure, I'll email that over today. It has a couple of new tips on screen pop timing that might be useful.

26
00:03:25.109 --> 00:03:26.366
Julie Hammond: Perfect. Thanks, Tom.

27
00:03:27.318 --> 00:03:32.448
Tom Lindqvist: No problem. I'll follow up with the training link and the doc. Talk soon.

28
00:03:33.722 --> 00:03:34.740
Julie Hammond: Sounds good. Bye.
